# {{Name}}

A Gerber Plugin API v1 module targeting PowerShell 7.4. No Azure, PAT,
customer configuration, or private Core API is required.

## Develop

Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for the canonical plugin development guide, public
API contract and agent-resource hierarchy. `CLAUDE.md` and GitHub Copilot
instructions point there; scoped instructions, a plugin developer agent and
three actionable skills live under `.github/`.

Install the development dependency only if missing:

```powershell
Install-Module -Name NovaModuleTools
```

From this directory:

```powershell
./scripts/Test-PluginBoundary.ps1
Invoke-NovaBuild
Invoke-NovaTest
Test-NovaBuild
Publish-NovaModule -Local
```

The boundary script uses the installed Gerber public command without starting
Gerber or installing this plugin. Inspect current capabilities with
`(Test-GerberPluginBoundary -Path .).PublicApi`. Fix diagnostics using that
public contract; request a new capability when none fits. Do not import private
Core files as a workaround. This static development check is not a sandbox and
cannot prove computed command targets safe.

Nova generates `dist/{{Name}}/{{Name}}.psd1` and `.psm1` from
`project.json`, `src/public/` and `src/private/`. Do not hand-author those artifacts.
Keep the manifest GUID `{{Guid}}` stable when updating this plugin.
`Manifest.PrivateData.Gerber` declares API v1 and the minimum Core version.

Local publish builds/tests and copies the module into your PowerShell module
directory, replacing that module there. To isolate a test installation, use
`Publish-NovaModule -Local -ModuleDirectoryPath <isolated-directory>`.
It does not publish to a remote repository.

## Use

Restart Gerber after local publish, then enter:

```text
/{{Namespace}} hello
```

Expected screen: `Hello from {{Name}}!`

Gerber already approved, associated and enabled this generated manifest GUID.
Generation itself does not install or load the plugin. A separate Gerber user
configuration will request approval on first discovery.

## Tests and ownership

`tests/public/Get-GerberPlugin.Tests.ps1` tests source behavior.
`tests/public/Get-GerberPlugin.Integration.Tests.ps1` imports the built module,
checks its public entry point and metadata, and executes the registered hello
handler through supplied public UI operations. Core separately validates actual
registry registration before creation succeeds.

Gerber owns these initial plugin templates and the public API. Nova owns the
build, test, package and publish lifecycle. Add your own domain commands without
calling private Core functions.
